{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "notes": "Footsteps by armour weight (CireFootsteps). Every champion profile (ChampionRoster.json) and NPC archetype (NPCArchetypes.json) maps to a class; the native audio smoke fails if one is missing. Steps are synced to the body's real foot contacts: humanoid skeletons by foot-bone height (foot_l/foot_r), Bear and Centaur by their gait phase (UCireCreatureArt::MotionPhase, two diagonal contacts per cycle); bodies with neither fall back to a speed cadence (stride grows from strideWalk to strideRun cm between speedWalk and speedRun cm/s). Each layer picks a random member (surface-specific 'stone' / 'dirt' sets or 'any'), with random pitch, volume jitter and chance. The surface is traced under the foot: town meshes and the route road are stone, everything else is dirt; the Breach Fields default to dirt. cameraShake (cm) only applies to the local player's own body and only when Options > Audio > 'Heavy footstep camera shake' is on.",
  "maxDistance": 2800,
  "maxStepsPerSecond": 36,
  "volumeJitter": 0.15,
  "speedWalk": 250,
  "speedRun": 600,
  "classes": {
